label cyberland:
    show ishikawa smile
    with dissolve
    play music bgm3
    i "The cyber threat landscape."
    show ishikawa pointing
    with dissolveS
    i "This is the environment where cyber attacks happen."
    show ishikawa pointing smile
    with dissolveS

    i "It includes attackers,"  
    extend " their targets,"  
    extend " and the methods they use."
    show ishikawa
    with dissolveS
    pause
    show ishikawa smile

    i "Alright... let's go over it."
    show ishikawa armcross
    with dissolveS
    i "There are people behind these attacks."

    i "They are called threat actors."
    show ishikawa pointing smile
    with dissolveS
    i "They can be individuals,"  
    extend " groups,"  
    extend " or even organizations."
    show ishikawa
    with dissolveS
    i "And they all have different goals."
    show ishikawa armcross frown
    with dissolveS
    i "Some want money."
    
    i "Some want information."

    i "Some want to cause disruption."
    show ishikawa
    with dissolveS
    pause
    show ishikawa pointing smile
    i "So... what do they target?"
    show ishikawa frown
    with dissolveS
    i "Not just companies."

    i "Individuals are targets too."

    i "Personal data.\n"

    extend "Accounts.\n"

    extend "Devices.\n"
    
    i "Anything with value."
    show ishikawa armcross frown
    with dissolveS
    extend " And sometimes..."

    i "You are the easiest entry point."
    show ishikawa armcross
    with dissolveS
    pause
    show ishikawa pointing smile
    i "So... how do these attacks happen?"

    i "They use common methods."
    show ishikawa
    with dissolveS
    i " Phishing.\n"

    show ishikawa smile
    with dissolveS

    extend " Malware.\n"

    extend " Password attacks.\n"

    show ishikawa
    with dissolveS
    i "And other techniques."
    show ishikawa armcross
    with dissolveS
    i "Most of them don't start with systems."

    show ishikawa armcross smile
    with dissolveS
    i "They start with people."

    i "Simple actions..."
    show ishikawa smile
    with dissolveS
    i "Like clicking a link,"  
    show ishikawa armcross
    with dissolveS
    extend " or using a weak password..."

    i "Can be enough."
    show ishikawa smile
    with dissolveS
    extend" And the impact can be serious."
    show ishikawa pointing
    with dissolveS
    i "Data breaches.\n"

    show ishikawa pointing smile
    with dissolveS

    extend"Identity theft. \n"

    extend"Financial loss. \n"

    i "Or loss of access."
    show ishikawa armcross smile
    with dissolveS
    i "That's why awareness matters."
    show ishikawa armcross
    with dissolveS
    i "You don't need to be an expert."
    show ishikawa pointing smile
    with dissolveS
    i "But you need to understand the risks."
    show ishikawa smile
    with dissolveS
    i "Because security..."

    extend " Doesn't start with tools."

    show ishikawa
    with dissolveS
    i "It starts with behavior."
    show ishikawa armcross smile
    with dissolveS
    i "Remember this..."
    show ishikawa pointing
    with dissolveS
    i "Cyber threats are everywhere."
    show ishikawa pointing smile
    with dissolveS
    extend " But most of them..."

    extend " Still depend on one thing."
    show ishikawa
    with dissolveS
    pause
    show ishikawa smile
    with dissolveS
    i "Human mistakes."
    i "One of the most common attacks you’ll face is phishing emails."
    i "So how do you tell if an email is real or fake?"
    show ishikawa pointing
    with dissolveS
    i "First—check the sender’s address carefully."
    extend " Small misspellings or strange domains are a red flag."
    show ishikawa pointing smile
    with dissolveS
    i "Second—look at the message itself."
    extend " Real companies won’t rush you into urgent action."
    show ishikawa armcross
    with dissolveS
    i "Third—be careful with links."
    extend " If it looks suspicious, don’t click it."

    i "And finally—if something feels off..."
    show ishikawa pointing smile
    with dissolveS

    i "It probably is."
    stop music fadeout 1.0
jump tutorials

label phishing:
    show ishikawa armcross smile
    with dissolveS
    play music bgm3
    i "Phishing."
    show ishikawa pointing
    with dissolveS
    i "Phishing is a type of cyber attack that targets you."
    show ishikawa pointing smile
    with dissolveS 
    extend " Not your system."  
    extend " Not your firewall."  
    show ishikawa
    with dissolveS
    i "You."
    show ishikawa armcross
    with dissolveS
    pause
    show ishikawa armcross smile
    i "Alright... let's dive deeper into it."
    show ishikawa pointing smile
    with dissolveS
    i "Phishing refers to an attempt to steal sensitive information,"  
    extend " like usernames, passwords, credit card numbers,"  
    extend " and other important data."
    show ishikawa
    with dissolveS
    i "Attackers do this by pretending to be someone you trust."
    show ishikawa smile
    with dissolveS
    extend " Like a bank, a company, or a familiar service."

    i "The attacker lures the victim,"  
    extend " similar to how a fisherman uses bait to catch a fish."
    show ishikawa pointing
    with dissolveS
    pause
    show ishikawa pointing
    with dissolveS
    i "So... how is phishing carried out?"
    show ishikawa pointing smile
    with dissolveS
    i "First, the attacker sends a message."  
    i "Usually an email, but it can also be a text or chat."

    show ishikawa pointing
    with dissolveS

    i "The message often looks real and convincing."

    i "Then, the victim clicks the link or opens an attachment."

    show ishikawa pointing smile
    with dissolveS

    i "They are redirected to a fake website,"  
    show ishikawa armcross smile
    with dissolveS
    extend " that looks like a real one."
    show ishikawa smile
    with dissolveS
    i "The attacker collects the victim's credentials."
    show ishikawa pointing
    with dissolveS
    i "And lastly, the attacker uses those credentials"
    show ishikawa pointing smile
    with dissolveS  
    extend " to access real accounts."
    show ishikawa smile
    with dissolveS
    i "It's that simple... but that's not all."
    show ishikawa pointing
    with dissolveS
    i "Phishing doesn't just rely on fake websites."
    i "It also relies on human behavior."
    i "These attackers manipulate human emotions"  
    show ishikawa armcross smile
    with dissolveS
    extend " to make people act quickly without thinking."
    show ishikawa pointing
    with dissolveS
    i "The most common triggers they use are:"
    show ishikawa pointing smile
    with dissolveS
    i "Fear. \n"  
    extend "Urgency.\n"  
    extend "Greed.\n"  
    extend "Curiosity.\n"  
    i "And trust."
    show ishikawa
    with dissolveS
    i "Messages like:\n"
    show ishikawa smile
    with dissolveS
    extend "'Your account will be locked.'\n"  
    extend "'Act now.'\n"  
    extend "'You've won something.' \n"
    show ishikawa armcross
    with dissolveS
    i "These are designed to make you react fast."
    show ishikawa smile
    with dissolve
    i "But you can avoid it."
    show ishikawa pointing smile
    with dissolveS
    i "Always check the sender."

    i "Don't click links immediately."
    show ishikawa armcross
    with dissolveS
    i "If you're unsure,"  
    show ishikawa smile
    with dissolveS 
    extend " go directly to the official website instead."

    i "And never share your passwords."

    i "You can also use extra protection,"  
    show ishikawa armcross smile
    with dissolveS
    extend " like multi-factor authentication."
    show ishikawa
    with dissolveS
    i "But don't worry..."  
    show ishikawa smile
    with dissolveS
    extend " I will teach you how to fight against these phishing threats."
    stop music fadeout 1.0
jump tutorials

label cpassword:

    play music bgm3

    show ishikawa
    with dissolve

    i "Passwords."
    show ishikawa smile
    with dissolve
    i "Passwords are the first line of defense"
    extend " for your accounts and personal data."

    show ishikawa armcross
    with dissolveS

    i "But they are also..."
    show ishikawa armcross smile
    with dissolveS
    extend " one of the most common weaknesses."

    show ishikawa smile
    with dissolveS

    i "Alright... let's go over it."

    show ishikawa pointing
    with dissolveS

    i "A password is used to prove your identity."
    show ishikawa pointing smile
    with dissolveS
    i "It protects your accounts,"
    extend " your information,"
    extend " and your access."

    show ishikawa armcross frown
    with dissolveS

    i "But if your password is weak..."

    extend " It can be guessed,"
    extend " stolen,"
    extend " or cracked."

    show ishikawa frown
    with dissolveS

    i "And once that happens..."

    show ishikawa frown
    with dissolveS

    extend " Your account is no longer yours."

    pause

    show ishikawa pointing
    with dissolveS

    i "So... how do attackers get passwords?"

    show ishikawa armcross
    with dissolveS

    i "They don't always hack systems."

    show ishikawa armcross smile
    with dissolveS

    i "Most of the time..."
    extend " they go after the password itself."

    show ishikawa pointing
    with dissolveS

    i "They can guess simple passwords."

    show ishikawa pointing smile
    with dissolveS

    i "They can try multiple combinations"
    extend " until one works."

    show ishikawa frown
    with dissolveS

    i "This is called a brute force attack."

    show ishikawa armcross
    with dissolveS

    i "They can also reuse stolen passwords"
    show ishikawa armcross
    with dissolveS
    extend " from previous data breaches."

    show ishikawa armcross smile
    with dissolveS

    i "If you use the same password everywhere..."

    extend " One leak is enough."

    show ishikawa
    with dissolveS

    pause

    show ishikawa armcross
    with dissolveS

    i "And sometimes..."

    extend " You give it away without realizing it."

    show ishikawa pointing
    with dissolveS

    i "Like through phishing."

    show ishikawa smile
    with dissolveS

    i "So... what makes a password weak?"

    show ishikawa pointing
    with dissolveS

    i "Short passwords.\n"

    show ishikawa pointing smile
    with dissolveS

    extend "Common words.\n"

    extend "Simple patterns."

    show ishikawa armcross
    with dissolveS

    i "Personal information..."

    show ishikawa armcross smile
    with dissolveS

    extend " like your name or birthday."

    extend " Or passwords like..."
    extend " '123456' or 'password'."

    show ishikawa frown
    with dissolveS

    i "These are easy to predict."

    show ishikawa
    with dissolveS

    i "So instead..."

    show ishikawa smile
    with dissolveS

    i "Use longer passwords.\n"

    extend "Mix letters.\n"

    extend "Numbers.\n"

    extend "And symbols."

    show ishikawa pointing
    with dissolveS

    i "Avoid anything that can be guessed."

    show ishikawa pointing smile
    with dissolveS

    i "And don't reuse passwords."

    i "Each account should have its own."

    show ishikawa armcross
    with dissolveS

    i "If one gets compromised..."

    show ishikawa armcross smile
    with dissolveS

    extend " The others stay safe."

    show ishikawa
    with dissolveS

    i "You can also use a password manager."

    show ishikawa smile
    with dissolveS

    extend " So you don't have to remember everything."

    show ishikawa
    with dissolveS

    pause

    show ishikawa pointing
    with dissolveS

    i "And one more thing..."

    show ishikawa armcross frown
    with dissolveS

    i "Never share your password."

    i "Not with anyone."

    i "Not even someone who claims to be support."

    show ishikawa pointing smile
    with dissolveS

    i "No legitimate service will ask for it."

    show ishikawa
    with dissolveS

    pause

    show ishikawa smile
    with dissolveS

    i "Remember this..."

    i "A strong password is simple to create..."

    extend " But easy to ignore."

    show ishikawa armcross
    with dissolveS

    extend " And that mistake..."

    show ishikawa frown
    with dissolveS

    i "Is enough to lose access to everything."

    stop music fadeout 1.0

jump tutorials